hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “When one of you wakes up from his sleep, he does not dip his hand in his ablution until he has washed it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2","Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “When he gets up at night, he uses the siwak to clean his mouth.”"
"3","Ahmad bin Abdah Al-Basri told us, he said: Abba Hammad, he said: Ghaylan told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: I entered upon"
"4","Humayd ibn Masada al-Basri and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us on the authority of Yazid. He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Atiq told me, He said: My father told me, he said: I heard Aisha, speaking on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The siwak cleanses the mouth and pleases the Lord.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5","Imran bin Musa and Humayd bin Masada told us, saying: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Habhab told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have used the siwak more than you.”"
"6","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “If it were not that it would be difficult for the believers, I would have ordered them to use the siwak for every prayer.”"
"7","Ali bin Khashram Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Anba Isa, meaning Ibn Yunus, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, he said: I said to Aisha: What did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, start with when he entered his house? She said: “With the siwak.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Qurrah told us, he said: Humayd bin Hilal told me, he said: Abu Burdah told me On the authority of Abu Musa, he said: I entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with me were two men from the Ash’arites, one of them to my right, and the other to my left. And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained calm, and they both asked for action. I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they did not inform me of what was within themselves. I did not feel that they were asking for work. It was as if I was looking at his siwak under his lip, which had been trimmed. He said: “We do not or will not use it on We made whoever wanted it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, the Meccan reciter, informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The fitrah is five: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the armpits, and trimming the nails. And shaved the mustache.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10","Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The fitrah is five: circumcision, istihadah, and trimming the mustache.” “And trimming the nails, and plucking the armpits.”"
"11","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Mu`tamar told us, he said: I heard Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Five things are part of the fitrah: trimming the moustache, plucking the armpits, trimming the nails, getting one’s hair, and circumcision.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"12","It was read to Al-Harith bin Miskin, and I heard, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fitrah is cutting the nails, shaving the pubic hair, trimming the mustaches, and growing the beard.”"
"13","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi` told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Trim the mustaches and grow the beard.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"14","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Suhayb, on the authority of Habib bin Yasar, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever does not take something from what he drinks, is not one of us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"15","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja’far told us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “A time has been appointed for us in: narrate The mustache, clipping the nails, shaving the pubic hair, and plucking the armpits, should we not leave it for more than forty days?” And he said another time: forty nights."
"16","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “When the madhhab went further, he said: Then he went for his need while he was on some of his travels, and he said: Come to me.” With ablution, so I brought him ablution, so he performed ablution and wiped over his socks.” Sheikh Ismail said: He is Ibn Ja’far bin Abi Katheer, the reader. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"17","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Ja`far Al-Khutmi told us Umayr bin Yazid, he said: Al-Harith bin told me. Fudayl, and Amara bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Qarad, who said: “I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to solitude, and when he wanted a need he would go farther away.”"
"18","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba Isa bin Yunus, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: “I was walking with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to a people’s shed and urinated while standing, so I moved away from him, so he called me and I was at his side until he finished. Then he performed ablution and wiped over his socks.”"
"19","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Ismail, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he entered the toilet, peace be upon him, he said: “O God, I seek refuge in You from wickedness and evil things.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"20","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Do not face the Qiblah and do not turn away from it when defecating or urinating, but rather face toward the east or west.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"21","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Ghandar informed us, he said: Muammar informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you goes to the toilet, he should not face the Qiblah.” “But to make it rise or set.”"
"22","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of his uncle Wasi bin Hibban On the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: “I rose to the back of our house and saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on two blocks facing the house. The sanctuary for its need.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"23","Sulayman bin Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Bahz told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Sulayman, and Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “walked to a people’s desert and urinated while standing.” Solomon said in his hadith: “And he wiped over his socks,” and he did not mention Mansur of the survey (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"24","Al-Mu'mal ibn Hisham informed us, he said: Ismail informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Wa'il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “came to the wasteland of a people and urinated while standing.”"
"25","Ali bin Hajar bin Iyas told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “Who “He told you that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, urinated while standing, so do not believe him. He only urinated while sitting.”"
"26","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hasanah, he said: He came out Upon us is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in his hand was the shape of a paper, so he placed it, then sat down and urinated on it, and some of the people said: Look. He urinates like a woman urinates! So he heard him and said: “Do you not know what happened to the companion of the Children of Israel? If any urine got on them, they cut it off with scissors. So he forbade them and was tortured in his grave.”"
"27","Hannad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I heard Mujahid, speaking on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He passed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on two graves, said: “They are being tormented, and they are not being tormented in a major matter, but this man was not hidden from With his urine, and as for this man, he was walking around slandering, then he called for a wet stick and split it in two, so he planted one on this one and on that one. One, then he said: “Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they do not dry out.” Mansour disagreed with him. He narrated it on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and he did not He mentions a peacock"
"28","Yahya bin Durst told us, he said: Abu Ismail informed us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, that Abdullah bin Abi Qatada told him, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you urinates, he should not take his penis with his right hand.”"
"29","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “When one of you enters the toilet, he should not touch his penis with his right hand.”"
"30","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjis, The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should urinate in a hole.” It was said to Qatadah: What is disliked about urinating in a hole? He said: It is said that they are the dwellings of the jinn (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"31","Ayoub bin Muhammad al-Raqqi al-Wazzan told me, he said: Hajjaj, meaning bin Muhammad, told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Hakimah, daughter of Umaima, on the authority of her mother, Umaima bint Raqiqa, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a bowl made of sticks in which he urinated, and he placed it under the bed. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"32","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that “ He forbade urinating in stagnant water.”"
"33","Ali bin Hajar bin Iyas informed us, saying: I am Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath bin Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdul Allah ibn Mughaffal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “None of you should urinate while bathing, for most of it is obsessiveness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"34","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Husayn bin Al-Mundhir. Abi Sasan, on the authority of Al-Muhajir ibn Qunfud, that “he greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was urinating, but he did not respond to him until he performed ablution, so when He performed ablution and responded to it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"35","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Aqeel told us, he said: My grandfather told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Many, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Two people should not go out to the toilet and sit uncovering each other.” about their private parts, for God hates that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"36","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Qasim told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Iyad, on the authority of Abu Saeed, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade those who defecated from speaking, for God abhors that.”"
"37","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Hilal bin Ayadh, he said: Abu Sa`id told me, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Two men should not go to the toilet, revealing their private parts.” They talk, for God hates that.”"
"38","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh told us, he said: Abba Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Uthman ibn Sunnah Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade any of you to relish a bone or dung.”"
"39","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, he said: Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not cleanse yourself with dung or with bones, for they are food for your brothers among the jinn.”"
"40","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Abu Muawiyah, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, On the authority of Salman, he said: A man said to him: Your friend is teaching you even nonsense. He said: Yes. He forbade us from facing the Qiblah. By defecation or urine, or by cleansing ourselves with our oaths, or by being content with less than three stones.”"
"41","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, On the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you drinks, he should not breathe into his vessel, and when he comes to the toilet, he should not He touches his penis with his right hand, but does not wipe it with his right hand.”"
"42","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muslim bin Qart, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you goes to defecate, he should take three stones with him.” Let him use it properly, for it will reward him.”"
"43","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Abu Ubaidah did not mention him, but Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, that he heard Abdullah say: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the toilet and ordered me to I brought him three stones, and I found the two stones, and I looked for the third but did not find it, and I took dung and brought them to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, took the two stones, threw the dung, and said: “This is a rex.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"44","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Salamah bin Qais, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “When you perform ablution, perform witr.”"
"45","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Salamah bin Qays, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “If you perform the prayer, then perform the Witr prayer.”"
"46","Qutaybah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mu’adh, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: “Flexible.” Tell your wives to cleanse themselves with water, for I make them feel ashamed of it. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.”"
"47","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba Al-Nadr, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Maimunah, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “when he entered the toilet, I and a boy with me would carry a bowl of water, so he would clean himself with water.”"
"48","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “performed ablution, and when he cleaned himself, he rubbed his hand on the ground.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"49","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Ahmad told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Water cannot be made impure by anything.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"50","Hanad bin Al-Sari and Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, on the authority of Abu Usama, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far, on the authority of Abd God bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water and the animals and wild animals that accompany it. He said: “If the water is two small amounts, it will not carry impurity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"51","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, saying: Abba Hammad, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that a Bedouin urinated in the mosque, so some people rose up to him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave him and do not force him.” When he finished, he called for a bucket and poured it on him."
"52","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ubaida told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: A Bedouin urinated in the mosque, “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a bucket to contain water and poured it over it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"53","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, saying: A Bedouin came in... The mosque urinated and the people shouted about it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave him.” So they left him until he urinated. Then he ordered a bucket of water to be brought in. So he poured water on him.”"
"54","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim informed us, on the authority of Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid, on the authority of al-Awza’i, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A Bedouin got up and urinated in the mosque, and the people ate him, so the Messenger of God said to them: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Leave him and pour a bucket of water over his urine, for you were only sent to facilitate and were not sent to make it difficult.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"55","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba Isa bin Yunus, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “None of you should urinate in standing water and then perform ablution with it.” And Khalas said: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The same may be upon him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"56","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Yahya bin Atiq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should urinate in standing water and then wash with it.” Al-Nasa’i said: Ya’qub did not talk about this. Hadith except for a dinar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"57","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Saeed bin Salamah, that Al-Mughirah bin Abi Burdah, He told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: A man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, we are riding The sea, and we carry a little water with us. If we perform ablution with it, we become thirsty. Should we perform ablution with sea water? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is pure, its water is permissible.”"
"58","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Jarir, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He was the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: “O God, wash away my sins with water of ice and hail, and purify my heart from sins, just as You purified the white garment from \defilement\"""""""
"59","Ali bin Hajar bin Iyas informed us, saying: Anba Jarir, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began the prayer, he would be silent for a while, so I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God. What do you say in your silence between saying “Allahu Akbar” and reading? He said: I say: “O God, separate me from my sins as You have distanced between the East and the West. O God, purify me from my sins as a garment is purified.” White from filth, O God, wash me from my sins with snow, water, and hail.”"
"60","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Mas’ar and Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, said: “I used to drink while I was menstruating, so I handed it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he put his mouth on a place in me.” He drinks it, and I sweat while I am menstruating, so I hand it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he puts his mouth on a place in me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"61","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “I was sweating, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his mouth where I had given birth while I was menstruating, and I was drinking from the vessel.” So he places his mouth where I gave birth while I was menstruating.”"
"62","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Hamida bint Ubaid bin Rifa’ah, On the authority of Kabsha bint Ka’b ibn Malik, that Abu Qatada entered upon her and mentioned a word that meant it, so I poured water for him to perform ablution, and a cat came. So she drank from it, and the vessel listened to her until she drank. Kabsha said: He saw me looking at it, and he said: Do you wonder, my brother’s daughter? ! So I said: Yes, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not impure, but rather it is from the circumambulations and circumambulations performed upon you.”"
"63","Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Anas, he said: The herald of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us. He greeted him and said: God and His Messenger “forbid you from donkey meat, for it is an abomination.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"64","Ali bin Hajar bin Iyas informed us, saying: Abba Ali, meaning Ibn Mushar, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Razin, and Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Kitten. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a dog licks the bowl of one of you, let him spit it out, then wash it seven times.”"
"65","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Ziyad bin Saad told me, that Thabit was the client of Abd Al-Rahman bin Zayd told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a dog licks in a vessel... “One of you, let him wash it seven times,” Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me. Hajjaj told us: Ibn Jurayj said, Ziyad bin Saad told me, Hilal bin Osama told him that he heard Abu Salama tell on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Like him"
"66","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Abdah bin Suleiman, he said: Ibn Abi Orouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If a dog licks the bowl of one of you, let him wash it seven times, first \With dust\"""""""
"67","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If a dog licks the bowl of one of you, let him wash it seven times, one of them with dirt.”"
"68","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Adding an aside, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the killing of dogs, and permitted the killing of hunting dogs and sheep. He said: “If the dog licks the vessel, wash it seven times and rub the eighth time with dirt.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"69","Muhammad ibn Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I heard Ibn al-Munkadir saying: I heard Jabir saying: I fell ill and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me. May God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Bakr returned to me and found that I had fainted. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution and poured his ablution on me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"70","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Ma’an told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The men and women were They performed ablution during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"71","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that she told him that she She used to “bathe with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the same vessel.”"
"72","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Jabr told me, He said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to perform ablution with a shuttle, and bathe with five Makki.”"
"73","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jabr, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, saying: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to perform ablution with a shuttlecock and bathe with five shuttlecocks.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"74","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, then he mentioned a word that means, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Habib, he said: I heard Abbad Ibn Tamim, narrating on the authority of his grandmother, who was the mother of Amara bint Ka’b, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “performed ablution and was brought with water in a vessel, about Two-thirds of the tide.” Shu'bah said: Remember that he washed his arms and massaged them, and wiped the inside of his ears, but I do not remember that he wiped the outside of them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"75","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Alqama, on the authority of Abd Khair, he said: We brought Ali bin Abi A student prayed and prayed to purify himself, so we said: What should he do when he prayed? He only wants to teach us, “So a vessel containing water and a basin was brought, so he emptied the vessel onto his hand, washed it three times, then rinsed his mouth, and sniffed it.” Three times from the palm with which he takes water, then he washed his face three times, washed his right hand three times, and his left hand three times, and wiped his head once. One time, then he washed his right foot three times, and his left foot three times, then he said: Who would be pleased to know the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? And peace be upon him, and this is him.”"
"76","Suleiman bin Mansour Al-Balkhi told us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, and Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, and the wording is by Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah bin Waqqas, On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Actions are but by intention, and a person is only what he intended, so whoever it is.” His migration is for God and His Messenger, so his migration is for God and His Messenger, and whoever’s migration is for a worldly gain, or for a woman He marries her, and his migration is to where he migrated.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"77","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “No prayer will be accepted without purification, nor will charity be accepted without deception.”"
"78","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abd God, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they did not find water. “So a water bottle was brought and he put his hand in, and I saw water gushing out from between his fingers, and says: “Live, both pure and blessed by God.”"
"79","Al-Amash said: Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad told me, he said: I said to Jabir: How many were you? He said: “One thousand and five hundred.”"
"80","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, he said: I heard Hamza bin Al-Mughirah Ibn Shu’bah, narrating on the authority of his father, said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he said: “Stay back, O Mughirah, and go on.” O people, I left behind with a tool of water, and the people left, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went for his need, and when he returned, I went. I poured water on him, and he was wearing a Roman robe with tight sleeves. He wanted to take his hands out of it, but it became tight on him, so he took his hands out from under it. “Then he washed his face and hands, wiped his head, and wiped over his socks.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"81","Humayd ibn Masada told us, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, saying: Shu’bah narrated to me, on the authority of Malik ibn `Urfatah, on the authority of Abd Khair. He said: I witnessed Ali. He called for a chair and sat on it, then he called for water in a bowl, washed his hands three times, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed with his palm. One time three times, then he washed his face three times, washed his right hand three times, and his left hand three times, and wiped his head, then washed his feet with water. Three, then he said: Whoever is pleased to look at the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then this is the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"82","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Thabit, and Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: Some people asked The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Does any of you have water?” So he put his hand in the water. Water, and he said: “Perform ablution in the name of God,” and I saw water coming out from between his fingers until the last of them performed ablution. Thabit said: I said: Anas: How many do you think they are? He said: About seventy"
"83","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Zayd bin Aslam told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Shall I not inform you of the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? So he performed ablution once, once.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"84","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, who was shown The call, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He performed ablution, washed his face three times, his hands twice, washed his feet twice, and wiped his head. \twice\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"85","Humayd bin Masada informed us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Habib, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, on the authority of Ibn Aws bin Abi Aws. On the authority of his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “staying alone three times.”"
"86","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abba Ibn al-Mubarak, he said: Abba Al-Awza’i, he said: Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab told me, that Abdullah bin Omar, “He performed ablution three times. This is attributed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"87","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking him about ablution, and he showed him Three times, then he said: This is the ablution, so whoever does more than this has done wrong, transgression and injustice. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"88","Mahmoud bin Ghailan told us, Ali told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about ablution. He showed it to him three times, then said: This is how ablution, so whoever does more than this has committed evil, transgression, and injustice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"89","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Humsi informed us, saying: Uthman, meaning Ibn Sa`id ibn Katheer ibn Dinar, narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri said: Ata’ bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Humran, that he saw Uthman praying for ablution and he emptied his vessel on his hand. So he washed it three times, then he inserted his right hand into the ablution and rinsed his mouth, inhaled, and rinsed it out, then washed his face three times, and his hands up to the elbows three times, then he wiped his head, then he washed each of his feet three times, then he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever performs ablution like this of mine, then prays two rak’ahs without talking to himself, He will be forgiven for his previous sins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"90","Al-Haytham bin Ayyub told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, he said: Anba Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing ablution and washing his hands, then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed one scoop, and washed His face, washed his hands once, and wiped his head and ears once.” Abdul Aziz said: Someone who heard Ibn Ghaylan tell me about that: And he washed his feet (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"91","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution, put his hand into the vessel, sniffed the water and rinsed his mouth once.”"
"92","Musa bin Abdul Rahman al-Kufi told us, he said: Husayn bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, he said: Khalid bin Alqamah told us, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Ali, that he called for ablution, “so he rinsed his mouth and sniffed, and sprinkled it with his left hand, and did that three times. He said: This is purification.” The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"93","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, and Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abba Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. On the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever performs ablution, let him blow his nose, and whoever uses \Let him get nervous\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"94","Muhammad bin Zanbour al-Makki informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, that Muhammad bin Ibrahim, He narrated to him, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If one of you wakes up from his dream Then he should perform ablution and blow his nose three times, for Satan spends the night on his nostrils.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"95","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Qaridh bin Shaybah, on the authority of Abu Ghatafan, he said: I entered On Ibn Abbas, I found him performing ablution, so he rinsed his mouth and rinsed his mouth, then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Sprinkle two \Two or three adults\"""""""
"96","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu al-Zinad told us, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “When one of you performs ablution, let him put water in his nose and then blow it out.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"97","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Wakee’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit, on the authority of his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about ablution. He said: “Perform ablution thoroughly, and frequently inhale, unless you are fasting.”"
"98","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Malik bin Arfata, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Ali, that He rinsed his mouth and inhaled with one palm three times, then said: “Whoever is pleased to look at the purity of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then this is \His purity\"""""""
"99","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Shaybah told me, that Muhammad bin Ali, He told him, he said: His father Ali told me, that Hussein bin Ali said: Ali called me to perform ablution and I brought it to him and he washed his hands three times. before he put them in his ablution, then he rinsed his mouth three times, and blew his nose three times, then he washed his face three times, then he washed his right hand until the elbow three times, then the left hand likewise, then he wiped his head once, then he washed his right foot up to the ankles three times, then the left Likewise, then he stood up and said: Hand it to me, so I handed him the vessel that contained the remains of his ablution, and he drank from the remains of his ablution while standing, so I was amazed. When he saw my amazement, he said: “Do not be astonished, for I saw your father, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing the same as what you saw me doing,” he said with his ablution. Thus, he drank the remainder of his ablution while standing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"100","Qutaybah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Hayya, he said: I saw Ali, he performed ablution and washed himself. He washed his hands until he cleaned them, then he rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed his mouth three times, washed his face three times, washed his arms three times, then wiped his head. He washed his feet up to the ankles, then he got up and took the remainder of his purification and drank while standing, then he said: I would like to show you how the Prophet purified himself. May God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"101","0 101 102 0 102 Utba bin Abdullah Al-Marwazi told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, that he said: By Abdullah bin Zaid bin Asim, can you show me how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution? Abdullah bin Zaid said: Yes, so he called for ablution. He emptied it on his right hand and washed his hands twice, then rinsed his mouth and rinsed it out three times. Then he washed his face three times, then he washed his hands twice, up to the elbows, then he wiped his head with his hands, then he turned towards them and turned away. He began with the front of his head, then he took them to the back of his head, then returned them until he returned to the place from which he started, then he washed his feet.”"
"102","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us on the authority of Jaid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Marwan informed me Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Abi Dhubab, he said: Abu Abdullah Salem told me, meaning Silan, he said: Aisha was amazed at his honesty. And she would hire him, so she showed me how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution. He said: “So she rinsed her mouth and rinsed her hair three times, and washed herself.” She washed her face three times, then washed her right hand three times, and her left hand three times, and placed her hand in the front of her head, then wiped her head thoroughly. one to the back of it, then she passed her hands over her ears, then passed over the cheeks.” Salem said: I used to come to her while writing, and she would sit between My hand, and she talked to me, until one day I came to her and said: Pray for blessing for me, O Mother of the Believers. She said: What is that? I said: Free me. By God, she said: God bless you, and she relaxed the veil behind me, and I did not see her after that day."
"103","Mujahid bin Musa told us, he said: Abdullah bin Idris told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution, scooped a scoop, rinsed his mouth and sniffed, then scooped a scoop.” So he washed his face, then he scooped a room and washed his right hand, then he scooped a room and washed his left hand, then wiped his head and ears with the insides of them. With the two rings and the backs of them with his thumbs, then he scooped a room and washed his right foot, then he scooped a room and washed his left foot.”"
"104","Qutayba bin Saeed and Utbah bin Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Al-Sanabihi, and Utbah said in his hadith, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Sanabihi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the servant performs ablution If the believer rinses his mouth, the sins will come out of his mouth. If he blows his nose, the sins will come out of his nose. If he washes his face, they will come out. sins from his face until they come out from under the eyelids of his eyes, so when he washes his hands, sins come out from his hands until they come out from under him. the nails of his hands, so when he wipes his head, sins come out from his head until they come out from his ears, so when he washes his feet, they come out The sins started from his feet until they came out from under the nails of his feet, then his walking to the mosque and his prayer were voluntary for him.”"
"105","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, he said: Bakr bin Abdullah told us. Al-Muzani, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “performed ablution and wiped His forelock, his turban, and his socks.” Bakr said: I heard it from Ibn al-Mughirah."
"106","Amr ibn Ali and Humayd ibn Masada informed us on the authority of Yazid, who is ibn Zuray’. He said: Humayd narrated to us. He said: Bakr ibn narrated to us. Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Hamza bin Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, on the authority of his father, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lagged behind. So I stayed behind with him, and when he relieved himself, he said: “Do you have water?” “So I brought him a cleanser,” so he washed his hand and his face, then he went, lowering his arms, and he closed the sleeve of the robe and threw the robe on His shoulders, then he washed his arms and wiped his forelocks, his turban, and his socks.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He narrated this hadith, Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of Hamza bin Al-Mughirah, and he did not mention the turban (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"107","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, I heard Hamza bin Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, speaking on the authority of his father, said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he said: “Stay back, O Mughirah, and go on, O people.” So I remained behind with a tool of water, and the people left, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to fulfill his need. When he returned, I went to pour water on him. He was wearing a Roman robe with tight sleeves, so he wanted to take his hands out of it, but it became tight for him, so he took his hands out from under the robe and washed. His face and hands, and he wiped his head and his socks. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"108","Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Amer Al-Shabi, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, and on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, on the authority of a man, until he referred it to Al-Mughirah, Ibn Awn said: I do not memorize the hadith of that one. In this hadith, Al-Mughirah said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he struck my back with a stick that he had, so he made amends and I made amends with him. Until we came to such-and-such on the land, but he did not fail. Then he set off until he disappeared, then he came and said: “Do you have water?” and I had a bowl of mine, so I went to him. With it, I poured it on him, “So he washed his hands and face, and went to wash his arms, and he was wearing a Levantine robe with tight sleeves, so he came out He removed his hands from under the clothes, then washed his face and arms, and removed some of his forelock and his turban.” Then Ibn Aoun said: “I will not remember as much as I want. Then he wiped over his socks, then he said: “What do you need?” I said: O Messenger of God, I have no need, so we came and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf led the people. He prayed one rak'ah with them in the morning prayer, so I went to raise him up, but he stopped me, so we prayed as long as we had finished and made up what we had done before. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"109","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hushaym told us, Anba Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Amr bin Wahb told me Al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard Al-Mughira bin Shu’bah, he said: “Two qualities I do not ask anyone about,” after I witnessed it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. We were with him on a journey and he went out for a need, then he came and performed ablution and wiped the forelock and the sides of his turban and wiped over his socks. He said: And the imam’s prayer was behind the man from his flock. He said: I witnessed from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was on a journey, so the prayer came and he stopped. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon them, was upon them, so they established the prayer and led Ibn Awf, and he prayed with them. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and prayed behind Ibn Awf. What remained of the prayer, when Ibn Awf said the salaam, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and performed what he had done previously.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"110","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is bin Zurai’, Shu’bah told us, and Mu’mal bin Hisham told us, he said: Thana Ismail, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Woe to the followers of \fire\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"111","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, and Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, He said: Sufyan told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a people performing ablution, and he saw their heels waving, and he said: “Woe to the heels of the Fire! ablution"
"112","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abu Ja’far al-Madani told me, he said: I heard Ibn Uthman bin Hunaif, meaning Amara, said: Al-Qaisi told me that he was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and water was brought, and he said On his hands from the vessel, “So he washed them once, and he washed his face and his arms once, and he washed his feet with both his hands.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"113","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Al-Ash’ath told me, he said: I heard my father, He narrated on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “loved the well-being as much as he could of purifying himself and putting on his shoes.” And his dismounting,” Shu’bah said: I heard Al-Ash’ath, through Wasit, saying: The Tyman likes to mention all of his affairs. Then I heard him in Kufa, saying: Tyman loves as much as he can (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"114","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, and Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: Yahya bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Kathir, who was nicknamed Abu Hashim, and I am Qutayba bin Saeed, he narrated to us Yahya bin Sulaym, on the authority of Ismail bin Kathir, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you perform ablution, perform the ablution thoroughly, and move between your fingers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"115","Muhammad bin Al-Ala Abu Kurayb told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, Malik, and Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, On the authority of Ubaid bin Jurayj, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: I saw you wearing these Sabbath sandals and performing ablution in them. He said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, wears it and performs ablution in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"116","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba Isa bin Yunus, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Ali, he said: I was I believe that the soles of the feet are more deserving of wiping, to the point that “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping the outside of them.”"
"117","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Sawda, on the authority of Ibn Abd Khair, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali performed ablution So he washed the backs of his feet, and said: “If I had not seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, washing the backs of his feet, I would have thought that their bellies were more deserving.”"
"118","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, that He performed ablution and wiped over his socks, and it was said to him: Should you wipe? He said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, anointing.” Abdullah’s companions admired what Jarir said, and Jarir had converted to Islam before The death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was easy."
"119","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, On the authority of Urwah bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of his father Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he went out for a need. Al-Mughirah followed him with a vessel containing water, “so he poured water on him when he had finished his need, so he performed ablution and wiped over his socks.”"
"120","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ajra, on the authority of Bilal, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace “He wipes over the socks and the veil,” he said. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"121","Al-Hussein bin Abdul-Rahman told us, on the authority of Talq, who was Ibn Ghannam, he said: Zaida told us, and Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, on the authority of Bilal, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping on the socks”"
"122","Hanad told us, he said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Bilal, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “he wiped over the veil and socks”"
"123","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Harb bin Shaddad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Salamah, on the authority of Ja’far bin Amr bin Umayyah Al-Damri, on the authority of his father, that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He performed ablution and wiped over \the socks\"""""""
"124","Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim Duhaim and Sulayman bin Dawud informed us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Ibn Nafi`, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Bilal entered the markets and went. Because of his need, then they left. Osama said: So I asked Bilala: What did he do? Bilal said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to fulfill his need, then he performed ablution, washed his face and hands, and wiped his head over his socks, then \he prayed\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"125","Suleiman bin Dawud and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he “wiped on the socks”"
"126","Qutaibah told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abu Al-Nadr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in “wiping over the socks that there is no problem with it”"
"127","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba Waki’, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Huzayl bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “wiped over the socks and the sandals.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: We do not know. That someone followed Abu Qais on this narration, but the authentic report on the authority of Al-Mughirah is that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “wiped over the socks,” and by God I know (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"128","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymrah, on the authority of Shuraih bin Hani, he said: I asked Aisha about wiping over the socks, and she said: Go to Ali, for he is more knowledgeable about that than me. So I came to Ali and asked him about wiping. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ordered us to wipe over the resident for a day and a night, and the traveler for three days.”"
"129","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Asim, that he heard Zurr bin Hubaysh, speaking, he said: I came A man called Safwan bin Assal. I sat at his door and he came out and said: What’s the matter with you? So I said: I seek knowledge. He said: The angels spread their wings to the seeker of knowledge, satisfied with what he seeks. He said: What are you asking about? I said: About the socks. He said: When we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, he commanded us not to remove them for three days except in case of ritual impurity. But from defecation, urination, and sleep.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"130","Amr bin Yazid Al-Basri told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Maysarah, He said: I heard Al-Nazzal bin Sabra. He said: I saw Ali praying the noon prayer, then he sat to attend to people’s needs. When the afternoon prayer came, a jug of water was brought. So he took a handful of it and wiped his face, arms, head, and feet, then he took the rest of it and drank while standing, and said: People hate this. “And I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing it, and this is the ablution of one who does not do it.”"
"131","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Alqamah bin Marthad told us, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution for every prayer, so when it was the day of the conquest, he performed the prayers with one ablution, and he said Omar told him: You did something that you did not do, and he said: “You did it intentionally, O Omar.”"
"132","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Al-Hakam, On the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he performed ablution, he would take a handful of water,” and he would say it like this and describe Shu’bah. He sprinkled his private parts with it, so I mentioned it to Abraham and he liked it."
"133","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Malik bin Mughul told us, on the authority of Awn bin Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of his father, he said: I witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing ablution, and Bilal took out the remains of his ablution, so the people rushed to him, and the goat was placed for him, so he prayed. With men, donkeys, dogs, and women passing before him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"134","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perform ablution thoroughly.”"
"135","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Abu Jahdam told us, he said: Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah told me. Ibn Abbas, he said: We were sitting with Abdullah Ibn Abbas, and he said: By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not single us out for anything to the exclusion of people. Except for three things: “We were commanded to perform ablution properly, not to eat charity, and not to ride donkeys on horses.”"
"136","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Shall I not inform you of that by which God erases sins and raises ranks by means of performing ablution properly in the face of hardship? And the frequent steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer, that is the bond, that is the bond, that is the bond.”"
"137","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Sufyan bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Asim bin Sufyan. Al-Thaqafi, that they invaded the Battle of Silasil, but they missed the battle, so they remained stationed, then they returned to Muawiyah, and with him were Abu Ayyub and Uqba bin Amer, and Asim said: O Abu Ayyub, we missed the general invasion, and we were informed that whoever prayed in the four mosques will have his sins forgiven. He said: O my nephew, I will tell you something easier than that: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever performs ablution as he was commanded, and prays As he was commanded, he will be forgiven for his deeds.” Is that so, O Uqba? He said: Yes"
"138","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb al-Marwazi, called Turk, told us, he said: Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, on the authority of Rabia bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” He has eight gates of Paradise. He enters through whichever one he wishes,” on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Asad bin Musa, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, On the authority of Rabia bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris, and Abu Uthman, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"139","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Khalaf bin Khalifa, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he said: I was behind Abu Hurairah. While he was performing ablution for prayer, he would extend his hand until it reached his armpit. He said: I heard my friend saying: “The jewelery reaches from the believer wherever it is.” The ablution is complete.”"
"140","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He went out to the cemetery and said: “Peace be upon you, the abode of a believing people, and we, God willing, will join you. I wished I could I saw our brothers.” They said: O Messenger of God, are we not your brothers? He said: “Rather, you are my companions and our brothers who have not yet come, and I left them at the basin.” They said: O Messenger of God, how do you know who Who will come after you from your nation? He said: “Have you seen that if a man had a horse that was not covered with horseshoes, would he not know his horses?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “For they will come on the Day of The Day of Resurrection will be as white as a result of ablution, and I will spread them out over the basin.”"
"141","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, and Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan Al-Thawri, Malik bin Mughal, Zuhayr, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, and Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr He said: I asked Safwan bin Assal about wiping over the socks, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to command us when we were traveling. To wipe over our slippers and not remove them for three days when defecating, urinating, or sleeping, except in the case of ritual impurity.” The pronunciation is for Ahmed"
"142","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, that he heard Zirr bin Hubaysh, speaking He said: I came to a man called Safwan bin Assal, so I sat at his door, and he came out and said: What is the matter with you? I said: I seek knowledge. He said: The angels spread their wings to the seeker of knowledge, satisfied with what he seeks. He said: What are you asking about? I said: About the socks. He said: When we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, he commanded us not to remove them for three days except in case of ritual impurity. But from defecation, urination, and sleep.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"143","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: Ali said: I was a man Matha, and the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with me, so I was ashamed to ask him, so I said to a man sitting next to me: Ask him, and he asked him, and he said “In it is ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"144","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, he said: I told Al-Miqdad If a man approaches his family and he is harmed and does not have intercourse, then ask the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, for I am ashamed to ask him. That was while his daughter was under me, so he asked him, and he said: “He should wash his private parts, and perform his ablution for prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"145","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Suleiman told me, he said: I heard Mundhir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali, on the authority of Ali, who said: I was ashamed to ask the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about pre-dhiy for Fatima’s sake. So I ordered Al-Miqdad and he asked him? He said: “In it is ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"146","Qutaibah told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha bin Anas, that Ali, he said: I was a man in distress, so I was commanded Ammar bin Yassar asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about his daughter with me, and he said: “That ablution is sufficient.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"147","Othman bin Abdullah told us, he said: Umayyah told me, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: A soul told us, and he is Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Iyas bin Khalifa, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, that Ali ordered Ammar to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “He should wash his impurities and perform ablution.”"
"148","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, Al-Zuhri told us, he said: Sa`id and Abbad bin Tamim told me, on the authority of his uncle, he said: I complained to The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He does not leave until he feels a scent or hears a sound.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"149","Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Muammar narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you wakes up from his sleep, he should not put his hand into the vessel until it is poured over it.” three times, for he does not know where his hand has been.”"
"150","Bishr bin Hilal told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a man feels sleepy while praying, let him leave, perhaps he will pray for himself without knowing it.” On the authority of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman al-Taffawi, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “If one of you feels sleepy during his prayer, let him leave and sleep.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"151","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Ruq told me, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to kiss some of his wives, then pray, but he did not perform ablution.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This hadith was narrated by Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Urwa, and Yahya Al-Qattan said, This hadith of Habib, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, and this hadith of Habib, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who was praying even if blood dripped on the mat in drops. Almost nothing (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"152","Qutaibah bin Sa`id told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I used to sleep in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed my feet in his qibla, and when he prostrated, he winked at me, and I clenched my feet, so when he stood up, I spread them out, and the houses On that day, they will have no lamps.”"
"153","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard Al-Qasim, speaking, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I have You saw me lying on my bed in front of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, praying. When he wanted to prostrate, he squeezed my feet and I hugged them to me. Then he prostrates.”"
"154","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak and Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told us, and the wording is his. He said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I lost the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. One night, I started to ask for him with my hand, and my hand fell on his feet while they were upright, and he was prostrating, saying: “I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your anger.” By pardoning you from your punishment, and I seek refuge in you from it, I cannot praise you as you have praised yourself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"155","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Maan told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: I entered upon Marwan ibn al-Hakam and we mentioned what ablution is used for, and Marwan said: Whoever touches a man will remember him. Urwah said: I did not know that. Marwan said: Busra bint Safwan told me that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “If one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution.”"
"156","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of a lieutenant, he said: Abdullah bin Badr told me, on the authority of Qais bin Talq, on the authority of his father Talq bin Ali, he said: We went out as a delegation until we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we pledged allegiance to him and prayed with him. When he finished the prayer, a man came who looked like a Bedouin. He said: O Prophet of God, what do you see in a man who touches his penis during prayer? He said: “Is it more than a small piece of your food or a small amount of your food?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"157","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Mushar bin Abd al-Malik bin Sala’, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Abd Khair, he said: We prayed With Ali at dawn, when he said the salutation, he got up and we got up with him, and he started walking until he reached the spacious area, where he sat down and leaned his back against the wall, so he raised His head, and he said: O Qunbar, bring me the bowl and the basin. Then Qunbar came and said to him: Put the bowl down. He put the bowl down, then said to him: Pour. So he poured water on him, and he washed his hands three times, then he said: “Put down.” So he placed the rak’ah, put his right hand in, took a hand full of water, and rinsed it out three times. He inhaled three times, then he inserted his palm and washed his face three times, then he inserted his right palm and washed his right arm three times, then he inserted it and washed His left arm three times, then he inserted his right palm and spread his fingers out in the water, then he raised them and wiped them on his left palm as you would wipe them. With your hands with oil, then he wiped his head and ears with it, and washed his feet three times, then he put his right palm in and took a full cup of water and drank it. Then he turned to us and said: “This is the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I would like to show you it.”"
"158","Muhammad bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: My father, and others, told me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Hayya al-Wadi’i, He said: I saw Ali performing ablution, washing his hands three times, rinsing his mouth three times, blowing his nose three times, washing his face three times, and wiping his arms three times. His head, and he washed his feet three times, then said: “This is the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"159","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Malik bin Arfata, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Ali, that he was brought He took a chair and sat on it, then he called a pitcher with water in it and placed two palms over his hands, then he rinsed his mouth and nose with one palm three times, and washed himself. He washed his face three times, and washed his arms three times, and took some water and wiped his head, then one part of his forelock pointed to the back of his head. Then he said: I do not know whether to return them or not, and he washed his feet three times, then he said: “Who would be pleased to look at the purification of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace?” This is his purification.” Yazid bin Zuray’ disagreed with him, and he narrated it on the authority of Shu’bah."
"160","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Malik bin Arafat, on the authority of Abd Khair, He said: I witnessed Ali calling for a chair and sitting on it, then calling for water in a bowl, washing his hands three times, then rinsing his mouth and sniffing with one palm. Three times, then he washed his face three times, and his hands three times, then he dipped his hand in the vessel and wiped his head, then he washed his feet three times, then he said: Whoever is pleased to look at the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, this is his ablution.”"
"161","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abbad bin Ziyad told me, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of his father, he said: I remained behind with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted me during the Battle of Tabuk. He emerged, then returned to me with the tool, and I poured water at the hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as the Messenger of God did. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then he sprayed his nose, rinsed his mouth, and washed his face three times. Then he wanted to wash his hands before taking them out. The sleeve of his robe became tight, so he took his hands out from under the robe and washed his right hand three times, and his left hand three times. \And he wiped his socks and did not take them off.\"""""""
"162","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Abbad bin Ziyad, that Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah informed him, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah informed him that he had fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Al-Mughirah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appeared before the excrement, so I carried with me some medicine before the prayer. At dawn, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned to me, I took an acupuncture on his hands from the medicine. He washed his hands three times, then washed His face, then he went to pull his jibbah away from his arms, but it became tight as his jibbah had been, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, inserted his hands into the jibbah. Until he took his arms out from under the robe and washed his arms up to the elbows, then he showed him a male wiping over his socks.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"163","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Hamza bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left behind due to his need, so he said: “Is there a way to purify myself?” So I followed him with a basin containing water, “and he washed his hands.” And his face, then he went to lower his arms, and there was tightness in the hands of the robe, so he took his hands out from under the robe and washed his arms. Then he wiped over his turban and socks, then he rode.”"
"164","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ismail bin Aliya told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Amr bin Wahb, he said: We were at Al-Mughirah, and he was asked. He said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and when it was dawn, he struck the neck of my camel. So I thought that he had a need, so I went with him until he disappeared from the people and got off his mount. Then he set off and disappeared from me until I saw him, then he stayed. For a long time, then he came and said: “Do you have water?” I said: Yes, so I poured water on him. He washed his hands and washed them well, then he washed his face. Then he went, lowering his arms and wearing a Levantine robe with narrow sleeves and narrow edges, so he took his hand out from under it and washed. His face and hands. He said in the hadith: He washed his face twice, so I do not know whether it was like this or not. Then he wiped with his forelock and wiped over the turban. He wiped over his socks, then we rode. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"165","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Alqama, on the authority of Abd Khair, he said: We brought Ali bin Abi A student, and he prayed, so he called for purification, so we said: What should he do when he prayed? Then he described his ablution. He said: And he wiped his head once, and he said: “Who? He was pleased to know the ablution of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it is this.”"
